  "title": "Complexity of the H-factor problem.",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "An $H$-factor in a graph $G$ is a set of vertex-disjoint copies of $H$ covering all vertices of $G$.\n\nProblem Let $c$ be a fixed positive real number and $H$ a fixed graph. Is it NP-hard to determine whether a graph $G$ on $n$ vertices and minimum degree $cn$ contains and $H$-factor?",
